      },
      "per_column_invariance_explanation": "macro_ap / macro_f1 are computed per policy column from cosine(content, bank[j]), which does not depend on any other column, so they are EXACTLY invariant in K for both bi-encoder arms. Their flatness is arithmetic, not evidence. The paper's 'accuracy maintained at scale' claim is only falsifiable under a COMPETITIVE decision rule, which is what mean_rank_true, mean_pct_rank, macro_f1_top_t and distractor_steal_top1 measure.",
      "top_t_f1_confound": "macro_f1_top_t is NOT a clean scaling metric. The top-T rule emits exactly T predictions per row; at K=n_real all T land on real columns, but as distractors enter they consume slots, so mean_real_predicted_per_row falls and precision rises for free. macro_f1_top_t can therefore INCREASE with K while the ranking underneath degrades. Read it only alongside mean_real_predicted_per_row, micro_precision_top_t and micro_recall_top_t. The uncontaminated degradation measures are distractor_steal_top1 and mean_rank_true vs mean_rank_chance."
    }
  },
